PBL Phase 3: Project Development, Prototype, and Exhibition Preparation Purpose of Phase 3 
Phase 3 focuses on moving from research and planning into project development,  prototype creation, and exhibition preparation. 
At this stage, students should begin showing clearly: 
∙ What they are going to create 
∙ How their research supports their idea 
∙ What materials, equipment, space, or technology they need 
∙ How their project will work 
∙ How the project will be presented at the exhibition 
∙ What visitors will learn from the project 
The final exhibition should not consist only of written research. Each project should  develop into a model, prototype, website, experiment, business proposal,  interactive demonstration, or another clear exhibition product.
This work can later support the actual exhibition demonstration if appropriate  materials and equipment become available. 
